\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\njs=s.split('\u003cscript type=\"module\">')[1].split('\u003c/script>')[0]\nopen('/tmp/codex.mjs','w').write(js)\nEOF\nnode --check /tmp/codex.mjs && echo OK\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"description\">Only show timing hint on control changes\u003c/parameter>\n\u003c/tool>\n\u003ctool name=\"Artifact\">\n\u003cparameter name=\"action\">publish\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"file_path\">/mnt/user-data/outputs/worldmakers-codex.html\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"url\">https://claude.ai/artifact/Sy5appH1aUMsPrMR3ckvHw\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"favicon\">📚\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"title\">The Worldmaker's Codex\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"label\">Worldmaker's Codex + Tour studio\u003c/parameter>\n\u003cparameter name=\"capabilities\">{'downloads': True, 'sample': {}}\u003c/parameter>\n\u003c/tool>\n````\n\nThe codex now has a **🎬 Tour studio**. It runs a timed walkthrough of the codex, 60 seconds by default, and records it to an MP4 video plus an MP3 of the background music.\n\n**The cycle**\n- You can set the cycle length from 10 to 900 seconds, or tap 30, 60, 90, 120 or 300.\n- The stops can be:\n  - Highlights: 12 stops, about 5 seconds each at 60 seconds.\n  - The whole codex: 50 stops.\n  - One part.\n  - The 31 book webs.\n  - Your own picks.\n- Timing is either even slices or fitted to the length of each narration line.\n- A cycle can repeat up to 12 times, and each repeat is saved as its own recording.\n- With short stops, the storm re-forms faster so each shape finishes building in time.\n\n**AI guide**\n- **✨ Write script with Claude** asks Claude for one line per stop, each kept short enough to say in that stop's time. The lines connect from stop to stop like a gallery walk.\n- You can edit any line, and its word count against the time available updates as you type.\n- Read-aloud speeds up each line so it finishes within its stop.\n\n**Studio layout (in the style of FrameForge and your Tarot apps)**\n- A row of tarot cards shows the stops, each with a roman numeral, its emoji in the center and its part's color.\n- Below it is a FrameForge-style timeline with four tracks (stops, script, score, capture), a playhead, and an elapsed / total time readout. Click it to jump to a stop.\n- A live preview shows exactly the frame that will be recorded.\n\n**What gets saved**\n- **MP4 video**, in one of three styles:\n  - Broadcast: the 3D view with a tarot card that flips in at each stop, captions that highlight word by word, a timeline bar and the clock.\n  - The 3D view alone.\n  - A screen or tab capture.\n- The video uses the AAC codec order from your Evolution Atlas fix, so it should post to X. The studio tells you which format it actually got.\n- **MP3 background**, either a generated score or your own audio file. The generated score follows each part's key and chimes at every stop change. It fades out exactly at the end of the cycle.\n- The MP3 is tagged with your music credit: Aaron as inventor, Claude + Music History as co-authors via AI pair programming. That credit also appears on screen in the last few seconds.\n\n**Library (Workshop, then Library)**\n- Every recording is kept in your browser's storage.\n- Each one can be played, or downloaded as the MP4, the MP3, the script, or a zip bundle with everything.\n- You can download a list of all recordings as a .md file, or a full .json manifest.\n- It shows how much storage you're using, with a \"Keep storage\" button so the browser won't clear the files on its own.\n\n**Limits**\n- Browser read-aloud voices can't be captured inside the video file. To include narration, use the \"Screen or tab\" capture and share the tab's audio. Broadcast videos show the narration as captions instead.\n- Inside this viewer, MP3s download inside a zip, because the viewer doesn't allow .mp3 downloads directly.\n- The Claude script button asks your permission the first time and uses your own Claude usage. If it isn't available, it uses a script the codex fits itself.\n- I tested the timing logic, the MP3 encoder, the zip files and the MP3 tag in code. I couldn't watch a full recording play in a real browser, so tell me if anything is off.\n\n---\n\n## Added October 9, 2026: watch list shared by Aaron\n\n# Top orgs to watch for HTML/JS + Python code production\n\n## Tier 1: Must-watch public code orgs\n- 🟢 Google — strongest overall for HTML/JS + Python production\n- 🟢 Microsoft — strongest for developer tooling + JS ecosystem + Python enterprise adoption\n\n## Tier 2: High-value additions to review\n- 🟡 Amazon — huge Python + web + AI infra signal, but less public\n- 🟡 Walmart — strong operational / retail AI workflows, lower public OSS visibility\n- 🟡 UHG — high-value enterprise workflow + Python/data logic, but low public code transparency\n\n## Directional scorecard (10-point signal)\n| Org | HTML/JS | Python | Enterprise leverage | AI pair-programming relevance | Overall |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Google | 9 | 10 | 9 | 10 | 9.6 |\n| Microsoft | 10 | 9 | 9 | 10 | 9.5 |\n| Amazon | 8 | 9 | 10 | 9 | 8.6 |\n| Walmart | 6 | 7 | 9 | 7 | 6.8 |\n| UHG | 5 | 8 | 9 | 8 | 6.8 |\n\n## Quick SWOT\n### Google\n- Strengths: 🌟 Web platform, ML infra, Python ecosystem, standards\n- Weaknesses: ⚠️ Large fragmented public footprint\n- Opportunities: 🚀 AI-assisted coding, web runtime, Python + data tooling\n- Threats: 🧨 Ecosystem fragmentation, competition\n\n### Microsoft\n- Strengths: 🌟 VS Code, TypeScript, Playwright, Azure AI, developer tools\n- Weaknesses: ⚠️ Broad scope, platform overlap\n- Opportunities: 🚀 Copilot, IDE automation, AI pair programming\n- Threats: 🧨 Platform lock-in, competition\n\n### Amazon\n- Strengths: 🌟 Scale, Python backend, cloud infra, AI services\n- Weaknesses: ⚠️ Less public code visibility\n- Opportunities: 🚀 Bedrock/SageMaker/agentic infra\n- Threats: 🧨 Internal complexity, fragmentation\n\n### Walmart\n- Strengths: 🌟 Retail logistics, pricing, forecasting, operations\n- Weaknesses: ⚠️ Lower public OSS signal\n- Opportunities: 🚀 Agentic ops, merchandising copilots\n- Threats: 🧨 Legacy systems, slower public contribution velocity\n\n### UHG\n- Strengths: 🌟 Data-heavy rules workflows, claims, care operations\n- Weaknesses: ⚠️ Limited public code transparency\n- Opportunities: 🚀 Claims automation, workflow copilots\n- Threats: 🧨 Regulatory complexity, trust/security risk\n\n## Best watch order\n1. 🏆 Google\n2. 🏆 Microsoft\n3. 🥇 Amazon\n4. 🥈 Walmart\n5. 🥈 UHG\n\n## Bottom line\n- If you only watch two: Google + Microsoft\n- If you want a stronger practical “AI pair programming” review habit: add Amazon immediately\n- Walmart and UHG are worth watching for enterprise workflow + operational AI, even if their public code is less visible\n"</script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@12.0.2/marked.min.js"></script>
<script>
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
const ls={get(k){try{return localStorage.getItem(k);}catch{return null;}},set(k,v){try{localStorage.setItem(k,v);}catch{}}};
let toastT;function toast(m){const t=$('#toast');t.textContent=m;t.classList.add('show');clearTimeout(toastT);toastT=setTimeout(()=>t.classList.remove('show'),2800);}
const reduceMotion=matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
const EMO=/[\p{Extended_Pictographic}\u{1F1E6}-\u{1F1FF}\u{1F3FB}-\u{1F3FF}\u{E0020}-\u{E007F}️‍⃣]/gu;
const say=w=>w.replace(EMO,'').replace(/↔/g,'with').replace(/→/g,'to').replace(/[·|]/g,'').replace(/^[—–-]+$/,'').replace(/&/g,'and').replace(/[`*#]/g,'').trim();

let blocks=[],cur=-1;

/* ---------- render ---------- */
function render(md,name){
  narr.stop();
  const doc=$('#doc');
  doc.innerHTML=window.marked?marked.parse(md,{gfm:true,breaks:true}):'<pre></pre>';
  if(!window.marked)doc.querySelector('pre').textContent=md;
  // fold code blocks; they are never read aloud
  doc.querySelectorAll('pre').forEach(pre=>{
    const n=pre.textContent.split('\n').length,d=document.createElement('details');d.className='code';
    const s=document.createElement('summary');s.textContent=`Code, ${n.toLocaleString()} lines (not read aloud)`;
    pre.replaceWith(d);d.append(s,pre);
  });
  doc.querySelectorAll('table').forEach(t=>{const w=document.createElement('div');w.className='tbl';t.replaceWith(w);w.append(t);});
  doc.querySelectorAll('a[href^="http"]').forEach(a=>{a.target='_blank';a.rel='noopener';});
  // section list: turn headings and top-level headings
  const jump=$('#jump');jump.innerHTML='';let k=0;
  doc.querySelectorAll('h1,h2').forEach(h=>{
    const isTurn=/^(Turn \d+|Added )/.test(h.textContent);if(isTurn)h.classList.add('turn');
    if(h.tagName==='H1'||isTurn){h.id='sec-'+(k++);jump.append(new Option(h.textContent.replace(EMO,'').trim(),h.id));}
  });
  // readable blocks
  blocks=[];
  doc.querySelectorAll('h1,h2,h3,h4,p,li,tbody tr').forEach(e=>{
    if(e.closest('details.code'))return;
    if(e.tagName==='LI'&&e.querySelector(':scope>p'))return;
    let text='',segs=[];
    if(e.tagName==='TR'){
      const head=[...(e.closest('table').querySelectorAll('thead th'))].map(th=>th.textContent.trim());
      const cells=[...e.children].map(td=>td.textContent.trim());
      text=say(cells[0])+'. '+cells.slice(1).map((c,i)=>`${head[i+1]||''} ${c}`.replace(/\//g,' and ')).join(', ')+'.';
    }else{({text,segs}=wordify(e));}
    if(!text.replace(/[.\s]/g,''))return;
    e.dataset.blk=blocks.length;blocks.push({el:e,text,segs});
  });
  const words=blocks.reduce((a,b)=>a+(b.text.match(/\S+/g)||[]).length,0);
  $('#docMeta').textContent=`${words.toLocaleString()} words, about ${Math.max(1,Math.round(words/160))} min aloud`;
  const h1=doc.querySelector('h1');$('#docTitle').textContent=name||(h1?h1.textContent:'Document');
  cur=-1;scrollTo(0,0);
}
function wordify(root){
  let text='';const segs=[];
  const walk=node=>{
    for(const n of [...node.childNodes]){
      if(n.nodeType===3){
        const frag=document.createDocumentFragment();
        for(const w of n.nodeValue.split(/(\s+)/)){
          if(!w)continue;if(/^\s+$/.test(w)){frag.append(document.createTextNode(w));continue;}
          const s=document.createElement('span');s.className='w';s.textContent=w;frag.append(s);
          const spoken=say(w);if(spoken){if(text)text+=' ';const st=text.length;text+=spoken;segs.push({start:st,end:text.length,el:s});}
        }
        n.replaceWith(frag);
      }else if(n.nodeType===1&&!/^(UL|OL|PRE|DETAILS|TABLE)$/.test(n.tagName))walk(n);
    }
  };
  walk(root);return{text,segs};
}

/* ---------- narrator ---------- */
const narr={speaking:false,paused:false,id:0,voices:[],keep:null,supported:'speechSynthesis' in window,
  loadVoices(){
    if(!this.supported)return;
    const vs=speechSynthesis.getVoices().slice().sort((a,b)=>a.lang.localeCompare(b.lang)||a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
    this.voices=vs;const sel=$('#voiceSel'),prev=sel.value||ls.get('reader.voice');sel.innerHTML='';
    if(!vs.length){sel.append(new Option('Default voice',''));return;}
    vs.forEach(v=>sel.append(new Option(`${v.name}, ${v.lang}${v.localService?'':', online'}`,v.voiceURI)));
    const en=vs.find(v=>/^en(-|_)/i.test(v.lang)&&v.default)||vs.find(v=>/^en(-|_)GB/i.test(v.lang))||vs.find(v=>/^en/i.test(v.lang))||vs[0];
    sel.value=prev&&vs.some(v=>v.voiceURI===prev)?prev:en.voiceURI;
  },
  voice(){return this.voices.find(v=>v.voiceURI===$('#voiceSel').value)||null;},
  ui(){const b=$('#playBtn'),on=this.speaking&&!this.paused;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',on?'true':'false');b.textContent=on?'❚❚':'▶';
    b.setAttribute('aria-label',on?'Pause reading':this.paused?'Resume reading':'Read aloud');
    $('#now').textContent=this.speaking?`${this.paused?'Paused':'Reading'}: ${section(cur)}`:'Tap a passage to start there, or press play.';},
  start(i){
    if(!this.supported){toast('Read-aloud isn\'t available in this browser.');return;}
    this.halt();this.speaking=true;this.paused=false;this.speak(i);
  },
  speak(i){
    const b=blocks[i];if(!b){this.finish();return;}
    focus(i,true);this.ui();
    const myId=++this.id;speechSynthesis.cancel();
    const u=new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(b.text),v=this.voice();if(v){u.voice=v;u.lang=v.lang;}
    u.rate=+$('#rateIn').value;u.pitch=+$('#pitchIn').value;let last=null;
    u.onboundary=e=>{if(myId!==this.id||(e.name&&e.name!=='word'))return;const s=b.segs.find(g=>e.charIndex>=g.start&&e.charIndex<g.end);if(s&&s.el!==last){last&&last.classList.remove('on');s.el.classList.add('on');last=s.el;}};
    u.onend=()=>{if(myId!==this.id)return;last&&last.classList.remove('on');if($('#keepIn').checked)this.speak(i+1);else this.finish();};
    u.onerror=e=>{if(myId!==this.id||e.error==='interrupted'||e.error==='canceled')return;toast('Reading stopped: '+e.error);this.finish();};
    speechSynthesis.speak(u);
    clearInterval(this.keep);if(!(v&&v.localService))this.keep=setInterval(()=>{if(speechSynthesis.speaking&&!this.paused){speechSynthesis.pause();speechSynthesis.resume();}},10000);
  },
  halt(){this.id++;if(this.supported)speechSynthesis.cancel();document.querySelectorAll('.w.on').forEach(e=>e.classList.remove('on'));},
  finish(){this.speaking=false;this.paused=false;clearInterval(this.keep);this.ui();},
  toggle(){
    if(!this.speaking){this.start(cur>=0?cur:firstVisible());return;}
    if(this.paused){speechSynthesis.resume();this.paused=false;}else{speechSynthesis.pause();this.paused=true;}
    this.ui();
  },
  stop(){this.halt();this.finish();}
};
function section(i){const b=blocks[i];if(!b)return'';let best='';document.querySelectorAll('#doc h2.turn,#doc h1').forEach(h=>{if(h.compareDocumentPosition(b.el)&Node.DOCUMENT_POSITION_FOLLOWING||h===b.el)best=h.textContent.replace(EMO,'').trim();});return best;}
let userScrollAt=0;['wheel','touchmove','keydown'].forEach(ev=>addEventListener(ev,()=>{userScrollAt=performance.now();},{passive:true}));
function focus(i,scroll){
  if(blocks[cur])blocks[cur].el.classList.remove('reading');cur=i;const b=blocks[i];if(!b)return;b.el.classList.add('reading');
  if(scroll&&performance.now()-userScrollAt>4000)b.el.scrollIntoView({block:'center',behavior:reduceMotion?'auto':'smooth'});
}
function firstVisible(){const y=innerHeight*.2;const i=blocks.findIndex(b=>b.el.getBoundingClientRect().bottom>y);return i<0?0:i;}

$('#doc').addEventListener('click',e=>{
  if(e.target.closest('a,summary,details.code,button'))return;
  const b=e.target.closest('[data-blk]');if(!b)return;const i=+b.dataset.blk;
  if(narr.speaking)narr.start(i);else{focus(i,false);$('#now').textContent='Press play to read from here.';}
});
$('#jump').addEventListener('change',e=>{const h=document.getElementById(e.target.value);if(h){h.scrollIntoView({block:'start',behavior:reduceMotion?'auto':'smooth'});const i=blocks.findIndex(b=>b.el===h);if(i>=0){if(narr.speaking)narr.start(i);else focus(i,false);}}});
$('#openMd').addEventListener('change',async e=>{const f=e.target.files[0];if(!f)return;try{render(await f.text(),f.name.replace(/\.(md|markdown|txt)$/i,''));toast('Opened '+f.name);}catch(err){toast('Couldn\'t open that file: '+(err.message||err));}e.target.value='';});

if(narr.supported){narr.loadVoices();speechSynthesis.onvoiceschanged=()=>narr.loadVoices();}
else{$('#voiceSel').append(new Option('Read-aloud unavailable',''));$('#voiceSel').disabled=true;}
$('#voiceSel').addEventListener('change',e=>{ls.set('reader.voice',e.target.value);if(narr.speaking&&!narr.paused)narr.start(cur);});
$('#rateIn').value=ls.get('reader.rate')||'1';$('#pitchIn').value=ls.get('reader.pitch')||'1';
$('#rateIn').addEventListener('change',e=>ls.set('reader.rate',e.target.value));$('#pitchIn').addEventListener('change',e=>ls.set('reader.pitch',e.target.value));
$('#playBtn').addEventListener('click',()=>narr.toggle());
$('#stopBtn').addEventListener('click',()=>{narr.stop();if(blocks[cur])blocks[cur].el.classList.remove('reading');});
addEventListener('keydown',e=>{const t=(e.target.tagName||'').toLowerCase();if(['input','select','textarea','button','summary'].includes(t))return;if(e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();narr.toggle();}else if(e.key==='Escape')narr.stop();});

render(JSON.parse($('#mdData').textContent));
narr.ui();
</script>
